This function first calculates the new line number by adding the number of lines to scroll to the current line number. It then ensures that the new line number is within the bounds of the terminal grid. If the new line number is out of bounds, it is set to the closest boundary (0 or the maximum number of rows - 1).

Next, it checks if there is a non-empty cell in the new line. If there is, it sets the new column number to the column of the first non-empty cell.

Finally, it updates the cursor point to the new point and returns the updated `ViModeCursor`.
